    "content": {
      "question_html": "<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Write a recursive function that returns the nth Fibonacci number, where fib(0) = 0 and fib(1) = 1.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(4)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Explain one disadvantage of using recursion for this problem.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(2)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(c)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Describe how an iterative solution would avoid this disadvantage.</div><span class=\"q-marks\">(2)</span></div>",
      "question_image_url": null,
      "mark_scheme_html": "<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(a)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Example answer:</div></div>\n<pre class=\"q-code\"><code>function fib(n)\n    if n &lt;= 1 then\n        return n\n    else\n        return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)\n    endif\nendfunction</code></pre>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Function defined with a parameter</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Correct base case</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Two recursive calls with n − 1 and n − 2</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">Results added and returned</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(b)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">Each call adds a stack frame, and the same values are recalculated many times</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">so time and memory use grow very quickly and the stack may overflow</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-part\"><span class=\"q-part__label\">(c)</span><div class=\"q-part__body\">A loop keeps only the previous two values in variables</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"q-line\"><div class=\"q-line__text\">so it uses constant memory and each value is calculated once</div><span class=\"ms-codes\">(1)</span></div>",
      "mark_scheme_image_url": null
    }
  },
